        <article class=3D"col-md-9 col-sm-9 main-content" role=3D"main">
  <header>
    <h1>Privacy laws compliancy</h1>
    <p>Smart is committed to ensuring that our services comply with the Eur=
opean Union=E2=80=99s <strong><em>General Data Protection Regulation</em> (=
GDPR)</strong>
      and other regulatory frameworks. The publishers must make sure that a=
n appropriate legal basis has been granted to collect
      and process the users=E2=80=99 personal data. To help the publishers =
provide the appropriate datapoints.</p>
    <p>This page explains you how to comply with some of these legislations=
.</p>

    <ol class=3D"toc">
      <li>
        <a href=3D"https://documentation.smartadserver.com/displaySDK/priva=
cy.html#gpp">Global Privacy Platform (GPP)</a>
        <ol>
          <li>
            <a href=3D"https://documentation.smartadserver.com/displaySDK/p=
rivacy.html#gpp-cmp">Consent Management Provider (CMP)</a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <a href=3D"https://documentation.smartadserver.com/displaySDK/p=
rivacy.html#gpp-ids">User and App Identifiers</a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <a href=3D"https://documentation.smartadserver.com/displaySDK/p=
rivacy.html#gpp-location">Location retrieval</a>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href=3D"https://documentation.smartadserver.com/displaySDK/priva=
cy.html#gdpr">TCFv2 (GDPR EU)</a>
        <ol>
          <li>
            <a href=3D"https://documentation.smartadserver.com/displaySDK/p=
rivacy.html#consent-management-provider">Consent Management Provider (CMP)<=
/a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <a href=3D"https://documentation.smartadserver.com/displaySDK/p=
rivacy.html#gdpr-passing-user-consent">Passing user's consent to <strong>Sm=
art Display SDK</strong></a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <a href=3D"https://documentation.smartadserver.com/displaySDK/p=
rivacy.html#user-and-app-id">User and App Identifiers</a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <a href=3D"https://documentation.smartadserver.com/displaySDK/p=
rivacy.html#tcfv1">Note about TCF v1.1 support</a>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href=3D"https://documentation.smartadserver.com/displaySDK/priva=
cy.html#ccpa">CCPA (California)</a>
        <ol>
          <li>
            <a href=3D"https://documentation.smartadserver.com/displaySDK/p=
rivacy.html#ccpa-passing-user-consent">Passing CCPA consent string to <stro=
ng>Smart Display SDK</strong></a>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href=3D"https://documentation.smartadserver.com/displaySDK/priva=
cy.html#iosprivacydetails">iOS App Privacy Details</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href=3D"https://documentation.smartadserver.com/displaySDK/priva=
cy.html#automaticlocation">Automatic location retrieval</a>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </header>

  <section>

    <!-- GPP -->
    <h2 id=3D"gpp"><a href=3D"https://documentation.smartadserver.com/displ=
aySDK/privacy.html#gpp">Global Privacy Platform (GPP)</a></h2>
    <p>The Global Privacy Platform (GPP) is an IAB specification helping al=
l stakeholders in digital advertising to support regional privacy regulatio=
ns more easily.
      GPP streamlines the transmission of privacy and consent signals from =
sites and apps across jurisdictions to ad tech providers. You will find mor=
e information in our <a href=3D"https://help.smartadserver.com/s/article/Gl=
obal-Privacy-Platform-GPP" target=3D"_blank">Help Center</a>.</p>
    <p></p>
    <p>Since v7.21.0, the <strong>Smart Display SDK</strong> handles both T=
CFEU2 and USP1 frameworks via GPP, and rely on them to handle User ID shari=
ng and location retrieval. You will find more information below.</p>
    <div markdown=3D"span" class=3D"alert alert-info" role=3D"alert">
      <em class=3D"fa fa-info-circle"></em> Despite <strong>Smart Display S=
DK</strong> compliancy with GPP, it is still compatible with the older TCFv=
2 and CCPA frameworks, outside GPP. Note that, for ID sharing and Location =
retrieval, GPP will have priority.=20
        The <strong>Smart Display SDK</strong> will fallback on older TCv2 =
and CCPA frameworks only if there is no GPP string available, or if the CMP=
 implementation is broken.
    </div>
   =20
    <h3 id=3D"gpp-cmp"><a href=3D"https://documentation.smartadserver.com/d=
isplaySDK/privacy.html#gpp-cmp">Consent Management Provider (CMP)</a></h3>
    <p>The first step to apply any consent framework handled by GPP is to c=
ollect the user's consent about the use of his personal data.</p>
    <p>This can be done through a <em>Consent Management Provider</em> (CMP=
). A CMP is a technology interface (usually an SDK for Apps environment) pe=
rmitting
      apps developers to provide transparency and obtain consent where nece=
ssary for themselves and/or on behalf of their
      chosen third parties and to transmit informations about which vendors=
 and which purposes a user has consented to
      with vendors.</p>
    <p>We recommend you integrate any CMP of your choice <strong>as long as=
 it is compliant with IAB's framework</strong> and specifications since <st=
rong>Smart Display SDK</strong> will retrieve consent based on these specif=
ications:</p>
    <div class=3D"row">
      <div class=3D"col-md-3">
      </div>
      <div class=3D"col-md-6">
        <a href=3D"https://github.com/InteractiveAdvertisingBureau/Global-P=
rivacy-Platform/blob/main/Core/CMP%20API%20Specification.md" target=3D"_bla=
nk">
          <button type=3D"button" class=3D"btn btn-xl btn-success col-md-12=
" style=3D"background:#62A8EA">IAB In-App Reference CMP for GPP</button>
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class=3D"col-md-3">
      </div>
    </div>

    <h3 id=3D"gpp-ids"><a href=3D"https://documentation.smartadserver.com/d=
isplaySDK/privacy.html#gpp-ids">User and App Identifiers</a></h3>
    <p>As we are doing with TCFv2 compliancy since <strong>Smart Display SD=
K</strong> 7.15.0, some identifiers won=E2=80=99t be sent in the ad call wh=
en
      Smart is not given the user=E2=80=99s consent retrieved by GPP. The i=
dentifiers are the UID, the IFA, the IFV, and the DNTID. This happens if an=
y of the juridiction handled under GPP do not give the consent.
      As the <strong>Smart Display SDK</strong> currently handles TCFEU2 an=
d USP1 via GPP, if any of those reject the consent, the identifiers won't b=
e sent.</p>

    <h3 id=3D"gpp-location"><a href=3D"https://documentation.smartadserver.=
com/displaySDK/privacy.html#gpp-location">Location retrieval</a></h3>
    <p>Since <strong>Smart Display SDK</strong> 7.21.0, the location is not=
 sent in the ad call when Smart is not given the user's consent retrieved b=
y GPP. This happens if any of the juridiction handled under GPP do not give=
 the consent.
      As the <strong>Smart Display SDK</strong> currently handles TCFEU2 an=
d USP1 via GPP, if any of those reject the consent, the identifiers won't b=
e sent.</p>
    <p>You will find more information about automatic location retrieval <a=
 href=3D"https://documentation.smartadserver.com/displaySDK/privacy.html#au=
tomaticlocation">here</a>.</p>

    <!-- GDPR -->

    <h2 id=3D"gdpr"><a href=3D"https://documentation.smartadserver.com/disp=
laySDK/privacy.html#gdpr">TCFv2 (GDPR EU)</a></h2>
    <p>Under the GDPR, you must make certain disclosures to your users in t=
he <em>European Economic Area</em> (EEA) and obtain
      their consent to use, where legally required, their personal data (su=
ch as AdID) to serve ads or process some analytics.</p>
    <p><strong><a href=3D"https://www.iab.com/" target=3D"_blank">Interacti=
ve Adverstising Bureau (IAB)</a></strong> provides some tools to help you i=
n this process.
      You might want to read more about how GDPR applies for advertising on=
 <a href=3D"https://iabeurope.eu/transparency-consent-framework/" target=3D=
"_blank">iabeurope.eu/transparency-consent-framework</a>.</p>

